CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT_ULL macro
#130: FILE: drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/x86-stub.c:21:
+#define MAXMEM_X86_64_4LEVEL (1ull << 46)

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'buffer_start < LOAD_PHYSICAL_ADDR'
#172: FILE: drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/x86-stub.c:758:
+	if ((buffer_start < LOAD_PHYSICAL_ADDR)				     ||
+	    (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86_32) && buffer_end > KERNEL_IMAGE_SIZE)    ||
+	    (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86_64) && buffer_end > MAXMEM_X86_64_4LEVEL) ||
+	    (image_offset == 0 && !IS_ALIGNED(bzimage_addr,
+					      hdr->kernel_alignment))) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

